# FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
#
# NOTE: Most configuration is now centralized in root .env
# See ../../.env.default and ../../CONFIG.md
#
# This file is for frontend-specific variables that don't fit in root .env
# Or for local overrides during development.
#
# NOT READ ANY MORE. `vite.config.ts` sets `envDir: '../'`, so Vite resolves its
# env file against the repo root -- a `frontend/.env` is now read by nobody.
# Kept as a template only; move any override you keep here into the root `.env`
# with a `VITE_` prefix (which is what publishes it to the browser).

# Backend configuration is read from root .env file automatically
# If you need to override, set these here:
# VITE_BACKEND_HOST=localhost
# VITE_BACKEND_PORT=8080
